        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(signal): preserve native quote replies from agent sends",
        "body": "Related: #101380\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Signal replies could be delivered as ordinary messages instead of native quoted replies. This happened when the agent sent through the message tool without explicit reply metadata, and when the quote author/body needed by Signal was no longer available at delivery time.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe fix stays entirely inside the Signal plugin. It retains bounded quote context for inbound and outbound messages, carries the current Signal message into same-conversation message-tool sends, and lets the existing reply-mode policy decide whether to attach the native quote. Ambiguous or unavailable quote metadata still degrades safely to an ordinary message rather than quoting the wrong sender.\n\nThis is the Signal-only replacement for the broader cross-channel approach in #101380; it does not change core, Telegram, Discord, or other channel implementations.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSignal users now receive native quote blocks when an agent replies through normal delivery or the message tool, including after the quote context crosses the plugin's delivery boundary. Existing `replyToMode` behavior remains in control of whether replies are quoted.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before the final fix, a live Signal reply succeeded but its receipt contained no `replyToId` or native-reply status. The agent's message-tool call had sent only the response text, so Signal never received quote metadata.\n- Exact deployed head: `1f79cb28bedbe6cd72174ba4f1e3684495d5770f` (`2026.7.2 (1f79cb2)`).\n- Focused remote verification: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/signal/src/core.test.ts` passed 57 tests with 0 failures.\n- Live Signal round trip: the prompt `Native quote live proof 1f79cb2 ...` received `stacked-live`; Signal rendered the response with a native quote block referencing that exact prompt.\n- Net diff against `main`: 13 files, all under `extensions/signal/`; no core or other channel files changed.\n- Reviewer-visible screenshot is not included because uploading the local Signal conversation image requires separate approval. The live external-client state was inspected directly and is described above.\n",
